# Normalize line endings on the way into the repository.
#
# This project is edited from both Windows and macOS. Without this file,
# a round-trip through the Windows working copy rewrote whole files as
# CRLF, and git then reported them as fully rewritten: on 2026-08-27
# msc_commands.py showed 6,226 changed lines when only 82 were real, and
# csv_export.py/excel_export.py showed ~200 and ~284 changed lines when
# nothing at all had changed. That noise hides real edits during review,
# which is exactly when sensitive-data mistakes slip through.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores everything with LF in the repo while leaving
# each developer's working copy alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only launchers genuinely need CRLF in the working tree; cmd.exe
# can mis-parse LF-only .bat/.cmd files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.xlsx binary
*.db binary
*.pdf binary
